Issue title: Feature Request: Implement Selection API / selections for text-editable elements

[TARGET]
After a bit more digging, the [Selection API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Selection) would allow for more fine-grained control over getting and setting what text is selected on a page, including getting text from specific nodes, the direction the user selected the text, as well as a few other really handy tidbits.

Imo this would be best placed under the `Document` trait in `dioxus-document` as something like this:

```rust
pub trait Document: 'static {
    pub async fn selection(&self) -> Selection {
        // Query the document for the data, whether by JS or other methods
    }
}

struct Selection<'a> {
    direction: String,
    // Other Selection API Properties
    document: &'a dyn Document, // Reference to document to allow for editing of the current selection
}

impl Selection<'_> {
    pub fn direction(&self) -> &str {
        &self.direction
    }
    pub fn to_str(&self) -> &str { ... }
    pub fn collapse_to_end(&self) { ... }
    pub fn delete_from_document(&self) { .. }
    // rest of the methods as shown in the API
