Issue title: panicked at 'already mutably borrowed: BorrowError' on nested signal

[TARGET]
Here you update the value of a signal, inside the callback to update the value of the parent signal:
```rust
// takes out a mutable borrow of `todos_view`
todos_view.update(|todos| {
    let mut todos = todos.as_mut().unwrap();
    let pos = todos.iter().position(|t| t.id == input).unwrap();
    // tries to take out a mutable borrow of `todos[pos].done` and panics
    todos[pos].done.set(!(todos[pos].done)());
});
```

Not sure what your IDE setup is like. In mine, rust-analyzer helpfully points out that the `mut todos` is unnecessary. And indeed you're not actually mutating the list.
<img width="752" alt="Screenshot 2023-06-29 at 7 06 43 AM" src="https://github.com/leptos-rs/leptos/assets/286622/690b7ad5-4f2e-4d9a-b1ae-80190f2ad2b9">

If I replace `.update()` with its immutable-borrowing equivalent `.with()`, there is no panic.
```rust
todos_view.with(|todos| {
    let todos = todos.as_ref().unwrap();
    let pos = todos.iter().position(|t| t.id == input).unwrap();
    todos[pos].done.set(!(todos[pos].done)());
});
```

Basically, you can't nest a signal update inside a signal update. You can nest a signal update inside an access with `.with()`

Does that help?

